  "comment": "LunarBase interior (the purchased pack: local only, docs/design/lunar-base.md, docs/design/lunarbase-sprites.md). Draws an area's entrance room, a map made by hand, one screen like a Zelda dungeon's first room: every door in sight as you arrive. On its back wall the comms monitor, orange lights and a starfield window, casting a shadow; a cross of shiny square plates on the floor from door to door; the studded floor (our own tiles in the pack's colours: artwork/tiles/lunar_int_extra.png, stamped over) with cyan floor lights, orange couches, black-topped counters. The side walls are a strip in the outer half of their blocks, solid only there (BLK_WALL_W, BLK_WALL_E), with their shadow on the floor in the inner half. Its outer doors are closed walls in the map; level.c opens the ones the area's links ask for (the door pieces and their jambs). Without the sheet the build uses plain stand-ins.",
